### Manual walkthrough of the auth API (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client).
### Prereqs: docker compose up -d && ./mvnw spring-boot:run. Emails: http://localhost:8025

@base = http://localhost:8080
@email = merchant@example.test
@password = correct horse battery staple

### 1. Register (always 202)
POST {{base}}/auth/v1/registrations
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

### 2. Confirm email: paste the token from the Mailpit link (after "#token=")
POST {{base}}/auth/v1/email-verifications/confirmation
Content-Type: application/json

{"token": "PASTE_TOKEN"}

### 3. Login: stores the access token; the client keeps the sf_refresh cookie
POST {{base}}/auth/v1/token
Content-Type: application/json

{"email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}"}

> {% client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 4. Call a protected endpoint
GET {{base}}/admin/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5. Rotate the refresh token (cookie sent automatically)
POST {{base}}/auth/v1/token/refresh
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

> {% client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### 6. Logout
POST {{base}}/auth/v1/token/revocation
X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest

### Public keys
GET {{base}}/auth/v1/jwks.json
